1
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:50,370
<i>I won't let your deaths be meaningless</i>

2
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:56,500
<i>even if I'm the last one standing</i>

3
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:05,370
<i>In both hands, Gloria</i>

4
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:07,370
<i>What sings is Sieg</i>

5
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:12,580
<i>On my back, Flügel der Freiheit</i>

6
00:01:13,500 --> 00:01:19,450
<i>Clenched determination to my left chest</i>

7
00:01:19,450 --> 00:01:24,790
<i>What slashes across is Linie der Torheit</i>

8
00:01:25,450 --> 00:01:28,040
<i>Soaring across the azure skies</i>

9
00:01:28,040 --> 00:01:32,580
<i>Flügel der Freiheit</i>

10
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:51,290
"Smile"
"Assault on Stohess, Part 1"

11
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:56,200
That's it, Annie!

12
00:01:58,330 --> 00:02:01,250
I'd expect no less
from my daughter!

13
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:05,660
What are you doing, Annie?!
No resting!

14
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:23,160
"Wall Sina" "Eastern fortified city"
You mean you haven't heard?

15
00:02:23,160 --> 00:02:25,160
The Titan boy and the
big shots in charge of him

16
00:02:25,160 --> 00:02:27,790
"Stohess District"
are apparently being called to the capital.

17
00:02:27,790 --> 00:02:29,700
And they're passing
through this city today.

18
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:30,950
I see.

19
00:02:30,950 --> 00:02:34,160
Sounds like he'll get dissection
for sure this time around.

20
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:37,000
Whatever the case, I just hope
he passes through without a hitch

21
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,250
and has the gate
shut firmly behind him.

22
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:44,660
Did you just
mention sealing the gate?!

23
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:48,620
You would suggest that we
defile the walls even further?!

24
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:53,540
Maria! Rose! Sina!

25
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:58,410
To defile the three goddesses is to
commit an unpardonable transgression!

26
00:02:58,410 --> 00:03:01,040
They love and worship
the walls as gods.

27
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,040
Don't get involved.

28
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:05,120
Man. They're still around, huh?

29
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:07,410
Damn...

30
00:03:07,410 --> 00:03:11,290
Our only protectors are the walls!

31
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,660
"Stohess District"
"Military Police Branch"

32
00:03:17,450 --> 00:03:19,750
You're <i>finally </i>up.

33
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:24,040
You look so totally scary when you're
asleep that I couldn't wake you up.

34
00:03:24,040 --> 00:03:25,950
Sorry, Annie.

35
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:28,540
You've been slacking a lot lately.

36
00:03:28,540 --> 00:03:32,290
What's this? Are you mad already?

37
00:03:32,290 --> 00:03:34,290
She's antisocial, all right.

38
00:03:34,290 --> 00:03:38,790
Just leave her be.
She came here from Trost.

39
00:03:38,790 --> 00:03:41,950
She's the only one
here who's seen real action.

40
00:03:41,950 --> 00:03:46,160
It'll take time for her to recuperate.
She's just been through hell.

41
00:03:46,160 --> 00:03:47,750
Ah, I get it!

42
00:03:47,750 --> 00:03:50,370
You have a thing for her!

43
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,870
What can you possibly
like about this girl?

44
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:54,200
Hitch.

45
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:58,450
There's only one way a ditz like
you could get into the Military Police.

46
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:01,790
Oh? Whatever do you mean by that?

47
00:04:01,790 --> 00:04:02,660
--Say it to my face.

48
00:04:02,660 --> 00:04:04,500
--Enough, you two!
--Say it to my face.

49
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:11,660
Oh, take it easy, guys.

50
00:04:11,660 --> 00:04:15,330
I have actual work for you today,
instead of the usual odd jobs.

51
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:17,540
That's why I called you here.

52
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:21,910
It's to do with the Scout Regiment
group being summoned to the capital.

53
00:04:21,910 --> 00:04:26,250
They're passing through
this town's main street today.

54
00:04:26,250 --> 00:04:28,950
Military Police HQ will be
serving as their security escorts,

55
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:32,540
so we need only assist
while they pass through.

56
00:04:32,540 --> 00:04:35,910
Omni-directional mobility within
city limits is temporarily authorized.

57
00:04:35,910 --> 00:04:39,620
You'll follow beside the
convoy and help bolster security.

58
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:43,370
You'll also head to
the starting point by barge.

59
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:44,910
That is all.

60
00:04:44,910 --> 00:04:46,660
May I ask something, Sir?

61
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:48,790
Hmm? What is it?

62
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:52,200
What are we supposed
to protect the convoy from?

63
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:59,540
I've never heard of <i>anyone </i>inside
this wall defying the royal government.

64
00:04:59,540 --> 00:05:01,540
There may be petty criminals,

65
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:05,040
but I can't imagine actual
organizations trying anything

66
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,250
unless they're based
outside the wall...

67
00:05:07,250 --> 00:05:09,160
I'm not even sure
what motive they'd have.

68
00:05:09,160 --> 00:05:11,410
Oh, you're a serious one!

69
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:13,410
You're in charge now.

70
00:05:13,410 --> 00:05:17,000
The details are all in here.

71
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:19,410
Huh?

72
00:05:19,410 --> 00:05:21,910
We officers are busy enough as it is.

73
00:05:21,910 --> 00:05:24,750
Prove that you can handle this yourselves.

74
00:05:25,750 --> 00:05:28,870
But no screw-ups. Got it?

75
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:31,250
Sorry to keep you waiting!
Shall we continue?

76
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:33,870
Whose turn is it again?

77
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,000
Damn! This is messed up!

78
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:45,290
Yeah, this organization's
way more rotten than I'd imagined.

79
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:48,330
Well, that <i>is </i>why I chose it,

80
00:05:48,330 --> 00:05:52,790
but you get stuck doing all the
work when you're a rookie here...

81
00:05:52,790 --> 00:05:55,120
Man, why didn't anyone tell me?

82
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:56,580
Bastard...

83
00:05:56,580 --> 00:06:00,250
All he can think about is himself!

84
00:06:00,250 --> 00:06:03,120
Huh? What are you talking about, Marlo?

85
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:07,160
Choosing to join the Military Police
makes you no different from him.

86
00:06:08,870 --> 00:06:13,080
No. I'm nothing like you degenerates.

87
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:16,580
I came here to <i>fix </i>the Military Police!

88
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:20,750
Wow, Marlo!

89
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:23,120
I never took you for that sorta guy!

90
00:06:23,120 --> 00:06:25,450
How are you gonna fix it?

91
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:27,870
By getting to the top, of course.

92
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:30,290
Once I'm at the top, I'll fix the rules

93
00:06:30,290 --> 00:06:34,160
and make the dishonest
pay fairly for their injustices.

94
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,830
It's that simple!

95
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:41,120
I'll simply turn them back
into normal people. That's all.

96
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,950
Back into the people
they're supposed to be.

97
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,250
Oh, man! You're the real deal!

98
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:52,500
Sorry! I originally took
you for a stick-in-the-mud!

99
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:55,330
That's quite the noble goal.

100
00:06:55,330 --> 00:06:56,910
Good luck with that.

101
00:06:56,910 --> 00:06:58,330
I wonder.

102
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:02,660
If a do-gooder like you took charge,

103
00:07:02,660 --> 00:07:05,080
I think <i>that </i>would spell the end for us.

104
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:09,040
Oh, so you <i>can </i>talk?

105
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:12,200
I think you're an honest person.

106
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:14,540
Because you say honest things.

107
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:18,120
I know there <i>are </i>people like that.

108
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:22,500
It takes a lot of courage
to go against the flow.

109
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,120
I respect that.

110
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:28,540
It could just be that
you're all fools, though.

111
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:34,000
No, maybe <i>they </i>are,
but don't lump me in with them!

112
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:39,040
Enough of this chit-chat. Let's go!

113
00:07:44,330 --> 00:07:48,250
The escort wagons will pass through
the outer gate in forty-five minutes.

114
00:07:48,250 --> 00:07:52,040
When we get there, find your positions.

115
00:07:52,040 --> 00:07:54,040
--Understood?
--Yeah, yeah...

116
00:07:59,120 --> 00:08:00,950
Hey, now!

117
00:08:01,790 --> 00:08:03,410
What's that?

118
00:08:03,410 --> 00:08:05,330
That's <i>our </i>equipment!

119
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:07,040
Must be taking it into the interior.

120
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:11,700
Still, it's strange for the merchant
association to be involved.

121
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:14,330
Just what are they...?

122
00:08:21,410 --> 00:08:24,830
They're illegally selling
government-issued equipment?!

123
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:28,790
Hey, now! What about
our assignment?!

124
00:08:28,790 --> 00:08:32,120
Oh, man! He's the genuine article!

125
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:34,750
Well, for better or worse, we <i>do </i>have time.

126
00:08:34,750 --> 00:08:37,290
This'll make for some nice entertainment.

127
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,950
So, how about a drink?

128
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:52,450
Yeah? What do you want, rookie?

129
00:08:52,450 --> 00:08:57,370
I-It's against the law to
sell government property.

130
00:08:57,950 --> 00:08:59,370
So?

131
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:05,120
Government property is paid for
by the citizens' hard-earned tax money.

132
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,540
Therefore--!

133
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:12,000
Wow, a rookie blackmailing
his superior officers...

134
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,450
You got a bright future in store, you do.

135
00:09:17,450 --> 00:09:20,830
Go get yourself a girl or
somethin' and refresh yourself.

136
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:22,620
Wha...?!

137
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,040
W-Wait!

138
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:27,910
It's against the law to sell--

139
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:51,620
Hey!

140
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:58,290
You're under arrest for a treasonable
offense against a superior.

141
00:09:58,290 --> 00:10:00,620
D-Don't be stupid...
Such disrespect for the law...

142
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:02,250
...is perfectly acceptable.

143
00:10:02,870 --> 00:10:04,500
Here, anyway!

144
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:10,120
I think that's enough, don't you?

145
00:10:12,330 --> 00:10:14,160
So sorry about that!

146
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:17,290
It seems our idiot has caused you trouble...

147
00:10:17,290 --> 00:10:20,620
We'll teach him a lesson, don't you worry!

148
00:10:20,620 --> 00:10:22,080
Or...

149
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:27,830
...would you prefer to have an
even bigger problem on your hands?

150
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,870
Just this once.

151
00:10:31,870 --> 00:10:33,290
Yes, Sir!

152
00:10:36,200 --> 00:10:41,500
--Now, let's get that drink.
--Yeah. I'd say we earned it.

153
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:53,910
Go on.

154
00:10:55,290 --> 00:11:00,950
You're going to make the dishonest
pay for their injustices, right?

155
00:11:00,950 --> 00:11:04,750
I'm not against helping
you out with that...

156
00:11:17,040 --> 00:11:18,450
Damn it!

157
00:11:20,330 --> 00:11:23,750
You're certainly a hard worker, Missy!

158
00:11:23,750 --> 00:11:26,620
Oh, no, you're too kind!

159
00:11:29,700 --> 00:11:31,950
Those people you know...

160
00:11:32,750 --> 00:11:37,330
Those fools you mentioned earlier...
Would they have done it?

161
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:41,330
They might have.

162
00:11:45,410 --> 00:11:48,750
You mentioned going against the flow...

163
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:55,330
I guess I'm just another piece
of scum being swept away by it.

164
00:11:55,330 --> 00:11:56,950
I don't know.

165
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:03,330
But maybe that's just
the way ordinary people are?

166
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:06,120
Personally...

167
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:10,410
Even if it means being a
weakling swept up in the flow,

168
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:13,290
being seen as a person is all I want.

169
00:12:36,750 --> 00:12:38,160
Annie.

170
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,580
Hi.

171
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:54,870
Looks like you're
a full-fledged MP now.

172
00:12:56,330 --> 00:12:57,790
Armin...

173
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,750
Why are you dressed like that?

174
00:13:13,750 --> 00:13:15,830
I'm a cargo carrier.

175
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:20,410
I'm hiding ODM equipment
under this rain gear.

176
00:13:20,410 --> 00:13:21,830
See?

177
00:13:22,450 --> 00:13:24,290
What is this about?

178
00:13:24,910 --> 00:13:26,120
Annie.

179
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:29,620
Could you help us let Eren escape?

180
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:31,580
Escape to where?

181
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:33,870
Defying the government's orders...

182
00:13:33,870 --> 00:13:36,040
Where <i>is </i>there to run inside these walls?

183
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:38,580
We just need to hide him for a while.

184
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:41,830
We won't be explicitly
rebelling against the government;

185
00:13:41,830 --> 00:13:45,750
it'll basically be an act of defiance
by part of the Scout Regiment.

186
00:13:45,750 --> 00:13:49,250
We're going to buy enough time
to gather some things

187
00:13:49,250 --> 00:13:53,700
that will unquestionably overturn
the council's say in the matter.

188
00:13:53,700 --> 00:13:55,910
Overturn it?

189
00:13:55,910 --> 00:13:59,910
There's really something that handy?
How are you so sure?

190
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,580
I'm sorry. I can't say.

191
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:10,620
Sorry, but I can't accept.

192
00:14:10,620 --> 00:14:13,910
I won't tell anyone, though.
Good luck.

193
00:14:14,790 --> 00:14:16,080
Annie!

194
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,330
Please!

195
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:20,120
They're going to kill Eren!

196
00:14:20,910 --> 00:14:23,120
A bunch of people who know nothing

197
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:26,290
are unwittingly pushing humanity
toward the brink of self-extinction

198
00:14:26,290 --> 00:14:29,370
simply to save their own necks!

199
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:32,700
I realize it sounds less than convincing.

200
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:37,330
But, even so, we have no
choice but to bet everything now!

201
00:14:38,250 --> 00:14:41,950
Of course, we'll try
hard not to cause you trouble.

202
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:45,950
But we absolutely need the
Military Police's help

203
00:14:45,950 --> 00:14:49,250
to sneak him through
Wall Sina's security checkpoint.

204
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:51,950
This is our only option left.

205
00:14:52,950 --> 00:14:54,910
Tell me.

206
00:14:54,910 --> 00:14:58,370
Do I look like that
good of a person to you?

207
00:14:58,370 --> 00:14:59,910
A good person...

208
00:14:59,910 --> 00:15:01,910
Actually...

209
00:15:01,910 --> 00:15:05,950
I've never been fond
of phrasing it that way.

210
00:15:05,950 --> 00:15:08,410
Because, to me,
it feels like it's only used

211
00:15:08,410 --> 00:15:13,500
to refer to people you
use for your own convenience.

212
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:18,000
And I don't think there's
anyone who's convenient to everyone.

213
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:22,450
Which is why, if you do say no to this...

214
00:15:23,370 --> 00:15:27,950
...that'd make you a bad person in my eyes.

215
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:46,000
Okay.

216
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:53,580
I'll do it.

217
00:16:05,370 --> 00:16:07,700
We got through surprisingly easily...

218
00:16:07,700 --> 00:16:08,870
Shh!

219
00:16:08,870 --> 00:16:10,950
That's the mighty Military Police for you.

220
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:13,040
Goes to show what kind of work they do...

221
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:15,200
Don't look around at everything.

222
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:18,330
Let's just hope they haven't
realized Jean took my place.

223
00:16:18,330 --> 00:16:21,250
That definitely won't last for long.

224
00:16:21,250 --> 00:16:24,790
He and I look nothing alike.

225
00:16:24,790 --> 00:16:26,290
It'll be fine.

226
00:16:26,290 --> 00:16:30,500
You both have the same
sort of mean, nasty look to you.

227
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:32,500
I don't have his horseface!

228
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,540
Say...

229
00:16:33,540 --> 00:16:35,910
How were you planning to get over the wall

230
00:16:35,910 --> 00:16:38,660
if I hadn't agreed to help?

231
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:41,790
We were going to barge through using ODM.

232
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,120
That's crazy.

233
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:46,450
Couldn't you have just
escaped before reaching Stohess

234
00:16:46,450 --> 00:16:49,620
to avoid all this trouble in the first place?

235
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:52,080
Why'd it have to be here and now?

236
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:54,290
I felt this town's complex layout

237
00:16:54,290 --> 00:16:58,250
would make our body double
ploy more likely to succeed.

238
00:16:58,250 --> 00:17:01,790
Plus, acting dutifully and
keeping their defenses down

239
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:06,790
will buy us far more time to escape
than head-on opposition would.

240
00:17:07,830 --> 00:17:11,500
I see. Good point.

241
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,700
Oh! Over there!

242
00:17:25,830 --> 00:17:26,950
Here?

243
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:29,790
Yeah. We're going through here.

244
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:34,750
It's what's left of an underground
city they were planning to make.

245
00:17:36,290 --> 00:17:40,040
It leads to the vicinity of the outer gate.

246
00:17:40,040 --> 00:17:42,870
Really? That's amazing.

247
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:45,540
Annie?

248
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,330
Oh, man.

249
00:17:47,330 --> 00:17:50,620
Don't tell me you're afraid of dark,
cramped places or something...

250
00:17:51,790 --> 00:17:54,870
Yes. I am.

251
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:58,500
I doubt a brave, suicidal maniac like you

252
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:02,830
would understand how a delicate damsel feels.

253
00:18:05,450 --> 00:18:10,160
Any damsel who can flip a grown man
upside down isn't weak at all.

254
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,790
Cut the crap! Let's hurry!

255
00:18:12,790 --> 00:18:15,080
No. I'm not going.

256
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:18,160
I'm afraid to go down there.

257
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:21,750
I'm not helping unless we
stay above ground.

258
00:18:31,370 --> 00:18:34,620
Quit being stupid! Just get down here!

259
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:35,660
Stop screwing around!

260
00:18:35,660 --> 00:18:37,160
Eren! Don't shout!

261
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,540
I'm sure it's fine, Mikasa.

262
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:45,000
Because, for some reason,
this whole area...

263
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,910
...has been completely
deserted for a while.

264
00:18:54,950 --> 00:18:58,450
Man... That really hurts.

265
00:19:00,870 --> 00:19:06,830
At what point did you
start looking at me that way...

266
00:19:06,830 --> 00:19:08,290
...Armin?

267
00:19:09,500 --> 00:19:10,790
Annie...

268
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:15,700
Why did you have Marco's ODM gear?

269
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:23,120
It had all the same scrapes and bumps...

270
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:28,660
I could tell, because I'd
helped him do maintenance on it.

271
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:30,080
Yes...

272
00:19:30,830 --> 00:19:34,450
I found it and took it.

273
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:40,160
Then, those two Titans we captured alive...

274
00:19:40,160 --> 00:19:41,750
Was it <i>you </i>who killed them?

275
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:43,830
Who knows.

276
00:19:43,830 --> 00:19:46,450
But if that's what you
suspected one month ago,

277
00:19:46,450 --> 00:19:48,750
why didn't you do anything then?

278
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:51,500
Even now I can hardly believe it...

279
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:55,200
I just... wanted to believe
I had it all wrong...

280
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:57,200
That's why I didn't...

281
00:19:58,410 --> 00:20:02,120
Still... Back then...

282
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:06,500
The fact you didn't kill me back then...

283
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:10,540
...<i>is </i>why we're in this situation now.

284
00:20:18,450 --> 00:20:22,620
Yeah... I agree with all my heart.

285
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:27,200
I never imagined you'd
end up cornering me like this.

286
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:35,290
Why <i>didn't </i>I do anything then...?

287
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:37,040
Hold on, Annie!

288
00:20:37,040 --> 00:20:39,750
There's still a chance
you're going along with all this

289
00:20:39,750 --> 00:20:44,290
as part of some horrible, idiotic joke!

290
00:20:44,290 --> 00:20:46,200
Just get down here!

291
00:20:47,290 --> 00:20:50,500
There's something you can
prove just by coming down here!

292
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:53,370
Come down here and prove it!

293
00:20:53,370 --> 00:20:55,200
I can't go down there.

294
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:58,040
I'm a failed warrior.

295
00:20:58,040 --> 00:21:01,000
I'm being serious here!
This isn't funny!

296
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,250
Talk to us, Annie!

297
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:04,580
We can still discuss this as--

298
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:06,000
Enough.

299
00:21:06,580 --> 00:21:08,700
I can't listen to any more of this.

300
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,080
It's pointless.

301
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:15,580
I'm going to carve you up again...

302
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:17,580
...Female Titan!

303
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,290
Armin...

304
00:21:45,290 --> 00:21:49,160
It's nice I could be
a "good person" for you.

305
00:21:49,660 --> 00:21:52,790
For now, you've won your bet.

306
00:21:54,830 --> 00:21:56,700
But...

307
00:21:56,700 --> 00:21:58,790
...<i>my </i>bet...

308
00:21:58,790 --> 00:22:00,250
...begins now!

309
00:22:13,410 --> 00:22:14,830
Eren!

310
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,200
Mikasa?!

311
00:22:21,200 --> 00:22:22,830
It's too late...

312
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:57,750
<i>If, by chance, I'm not me</i>

313
00:22:57,750 --> 00:23:03,000
<i>then who's to say that you're you?</i>

314
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:08,290
<i>Can you pick up the pieces of your heart</i>

315
00:23:08,290 --> 00:23:13,410
<i>that fell apart like a broken sand castle?</i>

316
00:23:13,410 --> 00:23:18,410
<i>The voice of someone calling out</i>

317
00:23:18,410 --> 00:23:22,500
<i>changed into ringing in my ears</i>

318
00:23:22,500 --> 00:23:27,660
<i>It's as if time has stopped</i>

319
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:30,450
<i>Now wake up</i>

320
00:23:30,450 --> 00:23:35,750
<i>I made my way out of the deep darkness</i>

321
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:41,000
<i>I fled like a swift wind</i>

322
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:48,500
<i>We used to be like living corpses,</i>

323
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:50,540
<i>but now we head beyond the walls</i>

324
00:23:50,540 --> 00:23:52,580
<i>Let's meet again</i>

325
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:57,410
<i>in a place not on any map</i>

326
00:24:09,580 --> 00:24:14,500
The Female Titan was actually
Annie Leonhart all along.

327
00:24:14,500 --> 00:24:19,500
However, even when faced with her,
Eren is unable to transform.

328
00:24:19,500 --> 00:24:21,620
Because she's Annie.

329
00:24:21,620 --> 00:24:23,370
"Mercy"
"Assault on Stohess, Part 2"
